    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="18.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 18.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="18.1"><pb n="252" ed="#liebermann"/>[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18.1" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="252" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ cyricsceat to Martinus mæssan</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="18.1" corresp="#wit-k"><ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#VIAtr_18-1.robnote.fn.3"/><pb n="96" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ cyricsceat to Martinus mæssan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="166" ed="#rabin-doml"/>and cyricsceat to Martinus mæssan,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="253" ed="#liebermann"/>und Kirchengeld zum Martinsfest [11. November]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">and church-scot at Martinmas [11 November]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_18-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="97" ed="#robertson"/>And church dues at Martinmas.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="167" ed="#rabin-doml"/>and church dues by the Feast of Saint Martin,</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="253"><ref target="clause:IIEg_3">II Eg 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Eg. 3</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="29"><label>substantially repeats</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_2-2">II Eg 2.2–3</ref> <quote>The references in Wulfstan's codes for Æthelred and Cnut substantially repeated what Edgar had said</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="449"><label>expanded in</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_11-1">V Atr 11.1</ref> <quote>At this point VI Ethelred 18.1 adds “and church-scot at Martinmas”.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:ICn_10">I Cn 10</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 10: VI Atr 18:1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Only in K. Liebermann compares II Eg 3.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Saint Martin: November 11.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_18-1.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Satz fehlt Hs. D und V Atr, vielleicht von beiden nur übersprungen, weil er wie der vorige auf <hi rend="italic">mæssan</hi> endet</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The sentence is missing in MS D and in V Atr, perhaps merely skipped by both because, like the preceding one, it ends in <hi rend="italic">mæssan</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_18-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II Edg. 3.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VIAtr_18-1.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><label>⁊</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. D.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
